\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces $\text  {XMSS}^{MT}$ multi-tree structure with $d$ layers, each containing subtrees of height $h'$. (a)~The multi-tree signature consists of $d$ XMSS signatures, one per layer. (b)~The overall hypertree: each subtree at layer $j$ signs the root of a subtree at layer $j{-}1$. For example, with $h = 20$ and $d = 4$, each subtree has height $h' = 5$, supporting $2^{20}$ total signatures.}}{16}{figure.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:LAT}{{6}{16}{$\text {XMSS}^{MT}$ multi-tree structure with $d$ layers, each containing subtrees of height $h'$. (a)~The multi-tree signature consists of $d$ XMSS signatures, one per layer. (b)~The overall hypertree: each subtree at layer $j$ signs the root of a subtree at layer $j{-}1$. For example, with $h = 20$ and $d = 4$, each subtree has height $h' = 5$, supporting $2^{20}$ total signatures}{figure.6}{}}
